WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:10.379
"Thanks for walking me to work this morning, Mateo." Ally gulped.

2
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.374
"I guess it's time to face Melanie."

3
00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:19.740
"Just remember, she can't hurt you as long as other humans are around," Mateo said.

4
00:00:19.741 --> 00:00:24.115
"I'll come back later and walk home with you."

5
00:00:24.116 --> 00:00:29.361
Ally threw back her shoulders and marched bravely into the diner.

6
00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.279
Flo was behind the counter.

7
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.031
"Good morning, Flo," Ally said.

8
00:00:36.032 --> 00:00:38.538
"Who's cooking today?"

9
00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:41.400
"Randy," Flo said.

10
00:00:41.401 --> 00:00:46.478
"Isn't he operating Rolling Ray's while Barry is away?" Ally asked.

11
00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:51.917
"Ray decided to put the food truck in the garage for a few weeks," Flo said.

12
00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:56.137
"He needs Randy in the kitchen for now."

13
00:00:56.138 --> 00:01:00.285
"What about Melanie?" Ally asked innocently.

14
00:01:00.286 --> 00:01:03.108
"She's off today," Flo said.

15
00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:08.178
Ally sighed. "I'm safe for now," she thought.

16
00:01:08.179 --> 00:01:10.600
"But what about tomorrow?"

17
00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:16.979
Just then Phil entered. "Good morning, everyone!"

18
00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:22.219
"All alone today, Phil?" Flo asked. "Where's Tina?"

19
00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:27.314
"She's at the museum. She's talking with Dr. Lloyd about his research.

20
00:01:27.315 --> 00:01:32.100
She's very interested in what he does. I'll take a coffee to go, please."

21
00:01:32.101 --> 00:01:38.232
A moment later Ray came out of his office.

22
00:01:38.233 --> 00:01:41.968
Ally noticed a strange look on his face.

23
00:01:41.969 --> 00:01:45.109
"Are you okay, Ray?" she asked.

24
00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:51.757
Ray poured himself a glass of cold water, then sat at the counter.

25
00:01:51.758 --> 00:01:55.089
"I just got off the phone with the CEO of Big City Foods.

26
00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.360
They own some of the largest chain restaurants in the country."

27
00:01:59.361 --> 00:02:02.871
"People eat chains?" Ally asked.

28
00:02:02.872 --> 00:02:08.671
Ray laughed. "A chain restaurant is one with different locations.

29
00:02:08.672 --> 00:02:11.647
They all have the same name and menu."

30
00:02:11.648 --> 00:02:15.299
"Why did the CEO call you?" Phil asked.

31
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.564
"His friend told him about the diner.

32
00:02:17.565 --> 00:02:22.798
This friend praised our food, the decor, and the general feel of the place."

33
00:02:22.799 --> 00:02:27.545
"That was nice of the CEO to call to tell you that," Ally said.

34
00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:31.742
"It was," Ray said, "but that's not all he said."

35
00:02:31.743 --> 00:02:34.394
Ally was confused again.

36
00:02:34.395 --> 00:02:40.869
"He asked if I'd be interested in an opportunity to expand Ray's Diner into a chain," Ray went on.

37
00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:44.777
"Wow. What did you say?" Flo asked.

38
00:02:44.778 --> 00:02:47.096
"Nothing yet," Ray said.

39
00:02:47.097 --> 00:02:49.978
"The CEO will be in town in two days.

40
00:02:49.979 --> 00:02:52.738
He'll visit the diner, and we'll talk some more.

41
00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:57.956
I'm not sure what will happen, but let's make sure this place is spotless."

42
00:02:57.957 --> 00:03:01.296
Ray picked up a menu with stains on it.

43
00:03:01.297 --> 00:03:04.756
"One thing we'd better do is print some clean menus.

44
00:03:04.757 --> 00:03:09.694
Ally, can you please go to the copy shop and ask Eli to print fifty new ones?"

45
00:03:09.695 --> 00:03:15.204
"Sure," Ally said. "Mateo and I can stop there on our way home later."

46
00:03:15.205 --> 00:03:19.614
Ray frowned. "I'd rather you go now, and by yourself.

47
00:03:19.615 --> 00:03:25.003
We need the menus pretty quickly, and I want to be the one to tell Mateo about Big City Foods."

48
00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:31.249
Ally gulped. The thought of walking alone through town made her nervous.

49
00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:33.583
But she couldn't let Ray down.

50
00:03:33.584 --> 00:03:38.064
"Sure, I'll go now."

51
00:03:38.065 --> 00:03:45.226
Ally walked down the street, nervously reading the minds of everyone she passed.

52
00:03:45.227 --> 00:03:51.382
She was pretty sure that Melanie was the Jorgandian, but she was still reading minds, just in case.

53
00:03:51.383 --> 00:03:54.877
A woman carrying heavy grocery bags walked by.

54
00:03:54.878 --> 00:03:59.007
All she was thinking about was getting home.

55
00:03:59.008 --> 00:04:10.952
A man pushing a baby stroller was thinking about getting a cup of coffee.

56
00:04:10.953 --> 00:04:15.777
"So far, so good," Ally thought as she entered the copy shop.

57
00:04:15.778 --> 00:04:22.416
"No sign of Melanie or anyone else thinking Jorgandian thoughts."

58
00:04:22.417 --> 00:04:26.580
One customer was waiting ahead of Ally.

59
00:04:26.581 --> 00:04:32.079
Two more came in right behind her.

60
00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:40.497
Eli, Coach Cross' brother and the owner of the shop, was running around, making copies and helping a customer.

61
00:04:40.498 --> 00:04:49.421
"Eli looks really tired," Ally thought, watching pages fly out of one copy machine and into a stack.

62
00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:57.125
Finally it was Ally's turn. "Hi, Eli. Ray needs fifty copies of the diner's menu, please."

63
00:04:57.126 --> 00:05:01.760
Eli stared at Ally for a second, blinking his eyes.

64
00:05:01.761 --> 00:05:05.587
"I wonder if he feels okay," Ally thought.

65
00:05:05.588 --> 00:05:08.042
But then Eli snapped out of it.

66
00:05:08.042 --> 00:05:12.250
"Uh, sure. I can't do it right now. Come back tomorrow morning.

67
00:05:12.251 --> 00:05:15.733
Early, before opening. I'll be ready for you then."

68
00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:17.983
"Okay." Ally shrugged.

69
00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:20.654
"We usually just wait for the copies. But—"

70
00:05:20.655 --> 00:05:27.374
"You can't wait for them today!" Eli said sharply. "I'm . . . too busy."

71
00:05:27.375 --> 00:05:34.521
"Okay. No problem." Ally didn't want to argue since Eli obviously wasn't feeling well.

72
00:05:34.522 --> 00:05:40.252
"See you tomorrow."

73
00:05:40.253 --> 00:05:46.754
Back outside, Ally hurried along the quiet street, eager to get back to Ray's safely.

74
00:05:46.755 --> 00:05:51.339
But then, just as she was getting close to the diner, she froze.

75
00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:54.144
Someone was running straight at her.

76
00:05:54.145 --> 00:06:00.978
Ally gasped. "Oh no! Melanie!"

